  "english": "18. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Second [Sunday after Holy Cross]. Forefeast [Barekendan] of the Cross of Varag. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk]: The Hosts of Angels (Hreshtakatsn dasq).\n19. Monday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Fast. [Feast of] Mamas, etc. Canticle [Harts] Tone 2 [ak]: Holy God who created (Surb astvats ara).\n21. Wednesday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Fast. Canticle of Penitence [Harts apts.] Tone 5 [g3]: Blessed are you, Lord, and glorified (Orhnyal es ter ev paravorial).\n25. Sunday. Tone 6 [DZ]. Third [Sunday after Holy Cross]. Feast of the Holy Cross of Varag. The intervening eating period is eight weeks.\n\nOctober:\n2. Sunday. Tone 7 [GK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [gk]: Your Resurrection (Ezqo yarutiund).\n9. Sunday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Fifth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [gz]: The Myrrh-bearing [Women] (Yughaber), and Today the Resurrection (Aysor yarutiun), and With the Sign of the Cross (I khachanish).\n16. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Sixth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [bk]: Christ is risen (ZKristos yaryav), and In the Morning (Aravotyan).\n23. Sunday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Seventh [Sunday]. Discovery of the Cross.\n25. Tuesday. Tone 5 [GZ]. [Feast of the] Hyperichians. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [g3]: You, the righteous (Ezqez ardar).\n26. Wednesday. Tone 7 [GK]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [gk]: God most high (Astvats bardzr).\n30. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Eighth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [ak]: The wondrous angel (Sqancheli hreshtakn). See also the others according to the order.\n\nNovember:\n6. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Ninth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [az]: With the women (End kanaysn), and Who ineffably (Or anchart).\n13. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK]. Tenth [Sunday]. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk]: Your angel, O Lord (Hreshtak qo ter), to the end.\n14. Monday. Tone 1 [AZ]. [Feast of] Andrew the Commander, and his army, etc.\n15. Tuesday. Tone 2 [AK]. [Feast of] Adrianus, and his wife Anatolia, etc. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [g3]: Who [welcomed] the torments (Orq ztanjanqn).\n16. Wednesday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [dz]: Blessed are you in [all] (Orhnyal es ya...).\n17. Thursday. Tone 4 [BK]. Holy Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and Godgiven [Asdvadzador] the witness. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [dz]: [In you] we trusted (Husatsyalqn).\n19. Saturday. Tone 7 [GK]. All saints, old and new, known and unknown.\n20. Sunday. Tone 6 [DZ]. Eleventh [Sunday]. Forefeast [Barekendan] of the Fifty-Day [Yisnak] Fast. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [dz]: Blessed are you, Lord (Orhnyal es ter). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [dz]: Awesome (Ahavogin) and Who art above (Or i verd es).\n21. Monday. Tone 8 [DK]. Fast. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God.\n22. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Fast. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [dz]: Who in all things did show (Or yamenayni tsutser).\n27. Sunday. Tone 7 [GK]. First [Sunday of Yisnak]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 2 [ak]: Without beginning Word (Anskizbn band). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [gk]: Taking... (Areal...).\n28. Monday. Tone 6 [DZ]. [Feast of] Julian and Vasilouhi. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [dz]: Holy are you, Lord (Surb es ter).\n30. Wednesday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Canticle of Penitence [Harts apts.] Tone 5 [g3]: Who [delivered] the three youths (Or zeris mankunsn). See also the others in the First Volume, keeping the order of this place until the end.\n\nDecember:\n4. Sunday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Second [Sunday of Yisnak]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: Who are King (Or tagavord es). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [gz]: Glorified is your Resurrection (Paravorial e qo yarutiund).\n5. Monday. Tone 7 [GK]. [Feast of] Genarius the Bishop, and Mercurius the Soldier, and Yakovik [Jacob] and Iravapar [the Orthodox].\n6. Tuesday. Tone 6 [DZ]. [Feast of] Abgar the King.\n9. Friday. Tone 2 [AK]. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n11. Sunday. Tone 4 [BK]. Third [Sunday of Yisnak]. Forefeast [Barekendan] of St. James [Surb Hakob]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: Who [made your] servant (Or ztsarayi). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [bk]: They anticipated (Kankhetsin).\n18. Sunday. Tone 3 [BZ]. Fourth [Sunday of Yisnak]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [g3]: Glorified Son (Paravorial vordi). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [bz]: In the tomb (I gerezman), and They came to the tomb (Ekin i gerezmann), and The voice of good tidings (Dzayn avetavor), and Today they rejoiced (Aysor zvartchatsan).\n24. Saturday. Tone 1 [AZ]. [Feast of] David the Prophet, and James the Apostle.\n25. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK]. Fifth [Sunday of Yisnak]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [gk]: Existing before eternity (Nakhahavityan). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 2 [ak]: Wondrous Resurrection (Hrashali yarutiun).\n29. Thursday. Tone 7 [GK]. [Feast of] the Sons of Thunder [Boanerges]. Forefeast [Barekendan] of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\nJanuary:\n1. Sunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Sixth [Sunday of Yisnak]. Fast. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [az]: Awesome vision (Soskali tesil), to the end.\n2. Monday. Tone 2 [AK]. Fast. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: Blessed are you, Lord God (Orhnyal es ter astvats).\n5. Thursday. Tone 5 [GZ]. Vigil [Chragaluyts] of the Nativity of Christ.",
